# Repo Wiki Curator

Continuous curation of the whole repository's documentation. Strategic objective and rules: **read first
[`docs/SCHEMA.md`](../../../docs/SCHEMA.md)** — this SKILL is the operational procedure of that constitution.

## Scope

All of `docs/` — `planos/`, `auditorias/`, `adr/`, `architecture/`, `design-system/`, `commercial/`,
`developers/`, `reunioes/`, `qa-evidence/`, `_arquivo/`. It is not just design-system (that is only one
category, with its own sub-schema in `docs/design-system/SCHEMA.md`). **Plus the repo-wide stray sweep:**
markdown scattered OUTSIDE `docs/` (repo root, `src/`, `backend/`, anywhere) is invisible to the wiki —
the lint reports each one as a `stray doc` WARN (curator inbox); classifying those into their category
box is part of this skill's job, not a separate task.

## Contract

1. **Read `docs/SCHEMA.md`** before touching any doc.
2. **Naming (SCHEMA §2):** lowercase `kebab-case`; the temporal class defines the date in the name —
   `living` = `slug.md` (no date), `event` = `YYYY-MM-DD-slug.md` (prefix), `sequenced` = `NNNN-slug.md`.
   Exceptions in caps: `README/SCHEMA/CLAUDE/AGENTS/LICENSE`. FULL-CAPS and Title-Case are violations.
3. **Frontmatter** (SCHEMA §3): `title/status/updated/scope`. `status ∈ {canon, active, superseded, historico, proposta}`.
4. **Dual temporal indexing** (SCHEMA §4): every `.md` in the category `index.md` + in the repo `docs/log.md`.
5. **Prune = git is the archive** (SCHEMA §5): resolved `superseded`/`historico`, PDF render, regenerable JSON and
   QA screenshots leave the working tree (git preserves them); never delete what still informs the current state.
6. **Never mark as `canon` a plan that the current code does not confirm.** The living truth = code, not the doc.

## Procedure

1. `find docs -name "*.md"` + `find docs -type f ! -name "*.md"` — inventory; compare against `docs/index.md`,
   `docs/log.md` and each category's `index.md`. **Repo-wide sweep:** the `stray doc` WARNs from
   `python3 .harness/lib/docs_wiki_lint.py` are the capture inbox for markdown living outside `docs/`.
2. For each doc: read title, verdict, date, execution status BEFORE classifying. Ambiguous/legacy →
   check against the real code (does the doc lie? does the code confirm it?). For each STRAY, decide its
   box — plan? audit? architecture? reference? junk? — then `git mv` it into `docs/<category>/` with §2
   naming (or `_arquivo/`); if it legitimately lives outside (e.g. a tool's own material), index it in
   place: cite the exact path or the collection (`dir/`) in `docs/log.md`/`index.md`.
3. **Naming:** rename violations with `git mv` (preserves history), **one at a time**, updating ALL the
   refs to it (`grep -rl` in the repo) before moving on — sequential migration (LEI ZERO §6), never batch.
   After the pass of renames/deletes, validate with `python3 .harness/lib/ref_integrity.py --range <base>..HEAD`
   (git-aware detector of orphan refs; correction protocol in the `ref-integrity` skill) — it is the guard that
   catches the forgotten citation the manual `grep -rl` let slip through.
4. Update `index.md` (category) + `docs/log.md` (`## [YYYY-MM-DD] type · category`, append-only).
5. Dense sub-wiki (design-system): also update `wiki/` and the specialized SCHEMA.
6. Prune the superseded/resolved (git rm) and record it in the log.
7. `python3 .harness/lib/docs_wiki_lint.py` — must be green (or justify the exception in the script itself).
   If the pass renamed/deleted files: `python3 .harness/lib/ref_integrity.py --range <base>..HEAD`
   green too (`.githooks/pre-commit` re-checks on the next commit, if `core.hooksPath` is
   pointed there — the `ref-integrity` skill covers the activation and the `use_pre_commit_framework` exception;
   the `.claude/loop.md` loop runs `--since` as a backstop independent of the local hook, only when
   `use_claude=true` — no native equivalent in Codex, see `docs/manual/15-limitacoes-conhecidas.md`).

## Expected output

- strays captured from outside `docs/` (from→to, or indexed-in-place with the reason);
- docs added/reclassified in the index (status);
- docs renamed (from→to) and refs updated;
- docs pruned (with how to recover via git);
- remaining naming backlog (what is left for future passes of the loop);
- result of `python3 .harness/lib/docs_wiki_lint.py`;
- result of `python3 .harness/lib/ref_integrity.py --range <base>..HEAD` when there was a rename/delete.

## Guardrail

Curation is incremental and continuous (runs in `.claude/loop.md` when `use_claude=true`; without that
runtime, an external cron calling the agent in non-interactive mode with the same checklist is the
equivalent). Do not do a mass effort of 80 renames in one turn — 1 category per pass, tested. The
objective is for the repo to become AI-navigable, not perfect all at once.
